xxt is an extremely small X11 terminal emulator. running memory usage recorded 1.6mb.
main.c is the original, unpatched xxt. every feature is a patch.

tldr:

	my config (copy/paste, blinking cursor, libvterm with scrollback, vi mode, curie font):
		patch main.c < patches/config.patch
		patch main.c < patches/copypaste.patch
		patch main.c < patches/blink.patch
		patch main.c < patches/libvterm-vi.patch
		sed -i 's|#define FONT ".*"|#define FONT "-*-curie-medium-r-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*"|' main.c
		cc -std=gnu89 -o xxt main.c -lX11 -lvterm -O2
		install -m 755 xxt /usr/local/bin/xxt

	curie: https://github.com/oppiliappan/curie
		install the font as described in its README, then check the name with
		`xlsfonts | grep -i curie`. if the wildcard above does not match, put the
		full name from xlsfonts into FONT. libvterm patches want an iso10646-1 font.

	just the original (no patches):
		cc -std=c89 -o xxt main.c -lX11 -O2

	smallest possible (194 lines, dumb terminal):
		patch main.c < patches/bare.patch
		cc -std=c89 -o xxt main.c -lX11 -O2

	patches stack, apply them in this order:
		1. config.patch                       always first, every patch except bare needs it
		2. copypaste.patch                    needed by scrollback, vi-mode, libvterm, libvterm-vi
		3. blink.patch, transparency.patch    any time after config, any order
		4. scrollback.patch and/or vi-mode.patch
		   or libvterm.patch                  (includes scrollback)
		   or libvterm-vi.patch               (includes scrollback and vi mode)

	not combinable: libvterm.patch / libvterm-vi.patch with scrollback.patch or
	vi-mode.patch or each other. bare.patch is used alone, on the original main.c.
	every valid combination and order was test-applied and compiled.

config (everything is a #define at the top of main.c):
	config.patch
		appearance	FONT BG_COLOR FG_COLOR
		window		WIN_TITLE WIN_CLASS FULLSCREEN WIN_WIDTH WIN_HEIGHT
		terminal	TERM_NAME DEFAULT_SHELL TAB_WIDTH BACKSPACE_CODE READ_SIZE
		also adds the small hooks the other patches build on
		(pixel_of, create_window, row_text, draw_span, draw_cursor).
	copypaste.patch
		MOUSE_SELECT MOUSE_PASTE_BUTTON MULTI_CLICK_MS WORD_CHARS COPY_ON_SELECT
		COPY_TO_CLIPBOARD SEL_CLEAR_ON_OUTPUT SEL_BG_COLOR SEL_FG_COLOR
		KEY_COPY KEY_PASTE KEY_PASTE_PRIMARY (each with a _MOD modifier mask)
	blink.patch
		CURSOR_COLOR CURSOR_STYLE (0 block, 1 underline, 2 bar) CURSOR_BLINK
		CURSOR_BLINK_MS CURSOR_THICKNESS CURSOR_UNFOCUSED_BOX
	transparency.patch   OPACITY
	scrollback.patch     SCROLLBACK WHEEL_LINES SCROLL_TAG
	vi-mode.patch        VI_ENTER_KEY VI_ENTER_MOD VI_SEND_ESC_MOD
	libvterm.patch       SCROLLBACK WHEEL_LINES SCROLL_TAG COLORTERM
	libvterm-vi.patch    all of the above plus VI_ALTSCREEN_PASS

patches:
	to apply a patch:
		patch main.c < patches/<filename>

	to remove a patch:
		patch -R main.c < patches/<filename>

	remove in reverse order, from an otherwise unmodified main.c.
	after applying or removing a patch, recompile.
	patching adds lines, so the size numbers below only describe the unpatched xxt.

	patches/config.patch
		moves the hard-coded settings of main.c into #defines at the top.
		fullscreen is a switch now. no behaviour change with the defaults.

	patches/copypaste.patch   (needs config)
		mouse: drag = select, double click = word, triple click = line.
		middle click pastes PRIMARY. selecting copies to PRIMARY.
		Ctrl+Shift+C copies to CLIPBOARD, Ctrl+Shift+V pastes CLIPBOARD,
		Shift+Insert pastes PRIMARY. other X11 apps can paste what xxt copies.
		the selection is cleared when new output arrives (SEL_CLEAR_ON_OUTPUT).

	patches/blink.patch   (needs config)
		blinking cursor. steady while typing. hollow box when the window is
		unfocused. block, underline or bar style.

	patches/transparency.patch   (needs config)
		background opacity via a 32-bit ARGB visual. text stays solid.
		needs a compositing manager (picom, xcompmgr, ...). without a 32-bit
		visual the window is simply opaque.
		set OPACITY (0-255) at the top, or XXT_OPACITY=<0-255> in the environment.
		selection and cursor colors are always opaque.
		with libvterm patches only the default background is translucent.

	patches/vi-mode.patch   (needs config + copypaste)
		vi-style keyboard navigation, selection and copy/paste, no new dependencies.
		works on the visible screen (with scrollback.patch also on the scrolled view).
		the mode and search prompt are shown in the window title.

		keys:
			Esc			input -> normal (VI_ENTER_KEY / VI_ENTER_MOD)
			Shift+Esc		send a real Esc to the shell (VI_SEND_ESC_MOD)
			i, q, Esc		normal -> input
			v, V			normal -> visual / visual-line (press again to cancel)
			Esc			visual -> normal

		normal and visual keys:
			h j k l, arrows		move
			w W b B e E		word motions
			0 ^ $			line start, first non-blank, line end
			gg G H M L		first line, last line, screen top / middle / bottom
			Ctrl-d Ctrl-u		half page down / up
			Ctrl-f Ctrl-b		page down / up
			f F t T ; ,		find character in line, repeat, reverse
			/ ? n N			search forward / backward, next, previous
			%			matching bracket
			counts			e.g. 5j, 3w, 10G
			o			visual: swap selection ends
			y, Enter		visual: yank selection and return to input
			yy, Y			normal: yank line(s)
			p			normal: paste clipboard into the shell, return to input

		yanked text goes to PRIMARY and CLIPBOARD.

	patches/scrollback.patch   (needs config + copypaste)
		scrollback buffer (10000 lines, plain text, SCROLLBACK). no new dependencies.
		Shift+PageUp / Shift+PageDown	scroll half a screen
		Shift+Home / Shift+End		oldest line / back to the bottom
		mouse wheel			scroll WHEEL_LINES lines
		typing jumps back to the bottom. scrolling clears the mouse selection.
		the top-right corner shows [offset/total] while scrolled.

	patches/libvterm.patch   (needs config + copypaste)
		replaces the built-in escape parser with libvterm (0.3+).
		16/256/truecolor, bold, underline, strikethrough, reverse, alternate screen,
		cursor visibility, UTF-8 (needs an iso10646-1 font), TERM=xterm-256color,
		function keys, modifier keys, application cursor mode.
		includes scrollback (2000 lines with colors), same keys as scrollback.patch.
		mouse selection and clipboard work on the scrolled view too.
		extra dependency: libvterm. libvterm.h uses inline: use -std=gnu89.

	patches/libvterm-vi.patch   (needs config + copypaste)
		libvterm.patch + vi mode in one patch. same vi keys as vi-mode.patch.
		Esc enters normal mode, Shift+Esc sends a real Esc.
		while a full-screen program (vim, less) uses the alternate screen, Esc goes
		to the program (VI_ALTSCREEN_PASS 1; set 0 to always enter vi mode).
		vi works on the scrolled view and yanks UTF-8.

	patches/bare.patch
		strips xxt down to 194 lines. dumb terminal: TERM=dumb, escape
		sequences are ignored, no resize, no arrow keys, no window close handling.
		line editing in the shell still works. full-screen programs do not.
		conflicts with all other patches, use it alone. Only choose this if you are trying to run xxt on a toaster.

compile:
	cc -std=c89 -o xxt main.c -lX11 -O2

	with libvterm.patch or libvterm-vi.patch:
		cc -std=gnu89 -o xxt main.c -lX11 -lvterm -O2

install:
	install -m 755 xxt /usr/local/bin/xxt

deps:
	libX11. POSIX PTY functions come from libc on glibc.
	libvterm patches also need libvterm.

